# Scout Report: toolkit (explore-codebase)

## 1. Overview

This is a Claude Code plugin toolkit that provides Agent Skills, sub-agents, hooks, and evaluation infrastructure. It functions as a comprehensive SDLC automation platform within Claude Code's plugin architecture. The project serves as both a development toolkit and a reference implementation for building Claude Code plugins.

## 2. Technologies

| Category | Technology | Version | Purpose |
|----------|-----------|---------|---------|
| Runtime | Claude Code (Node.js) | N/A | Plugin execution environment |
| Markup | Markdown/YAML | N/A | Skill definitions, agent configs, docs |
| Scripting | Bash | N/A | Hook scripts, validation utilities |
| Config | JSON | N/A | Plugin manifest, settings, hooks config |
| VCS | Git | N/A | Version control, worktree isolation |

## 3. Directory Structure

```
toolkit/
├── .claude/                    # Claude Code configuration
│   ├── agents/                 # SDLC sub-agents (HLD, LLD, IMP, TST, SRS, gate-verifier, sprint-master, tdd-backend, tdd-frontend)
│   ├── hooks/                  # Shell hooks (ensure-claude-md.sh)
│   ├── skills/                 # 14 Agent Skills (explore-codebase, skill-composer, skill-refiner, etc.)
│   ├── worktrees/              # Git worktree isolation directories
│   ├── hooks.json              # Hook registration manifest
│   └── settings.json           # Project-level settings
├── agent_docs/                 # AI agent reference documentation
│   ├── features/               # Feature requirement (FR-T-003.md)
│   ├── tech-design/            # Per-service technical design (sanitizer-service)
│   └── roadmap.md              # Roadmap for PaymentApp
├── docs/                       # User-facing documentation
│   └── skill-testing.md        # Skill testing documentation
├── evals/                      # Evaluation-driven development infrastructure
│   ├── explore-codebase/       # Eval configs and workspace for explore-codebase skill
│   └── orchestrator/           # Eval configs for orchestrator skill
├── scripts/                    # Utility scripts
│   └── validate-output-path.sh # Hook validation script
├── .work/                      # Working artifacts
│   ├── board.md                # Sprint board
│   ├── backlog.md              # Sprint backlog
│   ├── reports/                # Scout reports and exploration outputs
│   └── plans/                  # Execution plans
└── projects/                   # (empty) Reserved for project scaffolding
```

## 4. Modules and Responsibilities

| Module | Responsibility | Key Dependencies |
|--------|---------------|-----------------|
| `.claude/skills/` | Agent Skills - instructions for Claude to execute specific tasks | Independent per skill |
| `.claude/agents/` | SDLC sub-agents - specialized agents for design phases | Skills provide orchestration |
| `.claude/hooks/` | Automation hooks triggered by Claude events | settings.json for registration |
| `agent_docs/` | Reference docs for AI agents (architecture, features, tech-design) | None |
| `evals/` | Evaluation system for skill testing and benchmarking | Skills under test |
| `scripts/` | Shell utilities for validation and automation | None |
| `.work/` | Runtime artifacts (board, backlog, plans) | agent_docs, skills |

## 5. Entry Points

| Entry Point | Type | Path | Description |
|-------------|------|------|-------------|
| Plugin manifest | JSON | `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` | Plugin registration and metadata |
| Settings | JSON | `.claude/settings.json` | Project-level Claude Code settings |
| Hooks config | JSON | `.claude/hooks.json` | Hook event bindings |
| CLAUDE.md | Markdown | `CLAUDE.md` | Project instructions for Claude |

## 6. Dependencies

### Internal Dependencies

| Module | Depends On | Relationship |
|--------|-----------|-------------|
| Skills | .claude/agents/ | Skills spawn agents via Agent() tool |
| Hooks | .claude/settings.json | Registered via settings hook config |
| Eval | Skills | Tests skill behavior empirically |
| agent_docs | SDLC pipeline | Generated by SRS→HLD→LLD→IMP→TST agents |

### External Dependencies

| Package | Version | Purpose |
|---------|---------|---------|
| Claude Code CLI | N/A | Plugin host and execution environment |
| Git | 2.x | Version control, worktree management |
| Bash | 5.x | Hook script execution |

## 7. Architectural Patterns

**Plugin Architecture**: The project follows Claude Code's plugin architecture with `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` manifest and `skills/` directory for Agent Skills.

**SDLC Pipeline Pattern**: Skills spawn SDLC sub-agents (SRS, HLD, LLD, IMP, TST) in a sequential pipeline with gate verification between phases. This follows a document-driven SDLC approach where each phase produces structured documentation consumed by subsequent phases.

**Skill-Based Orchestration**: Skills act as orchestrators that spawn specialized agents. Skills provide the workflow logic; agents provide domain expertise. Skills use frontmatter to control invocation behavior.

**Agent Brief Pattern**: Agents receive input-only briefs (Context + Inputs + Task + Constraints) without output paths. Agents determine their own output locations based on their default templates.

**Gate Verification Pattern**: Each SDLC phase is followed by a gate-verifier agent that checks outputs against published criteria. Rejected phases trigger re-spawn with feedback. Maximum 3 re-spawns enforced.

**Evaluation-Driven Development**: Skills are tested empirically using evaluation infrastructure with Quick Workflow and Full Pipeline modes. Results stored in `evals/<skill-name>/workspace/iteration-N/`.

**Data Flow**: Human input → Skill (orchestrator) → Scout → Plan → SDLC Agents → Gate Verifiers → Sprint Integration → Summary. All agents read shared scout reports as foundational input.
